.TH PAPERSHELL 1 "2026-06-15" "GNU" "PaperShell Abbreviated User's Manual"
.SH NAME
PaperShell \- Swiss-Army knife for writing scientific papers in LaTeX
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B papershell
.I "[-h] [verb [noun ...]]"
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBPaperShell\fR is a LaTeX workflow for writing research papers that must be
submitted to different publishers (IEEE, ACM, Springer, Elsevier, AAAI, LIPIcs,
etc.) while keeping a single source document independent of the journal or
conference template. It allows you to switch between LaTeX document classes
(IEEEtran, acmart, llncs, elsarticle, lipics, …) without rewriting the paper,
and to export clean sources suitable for journal or conference submission.
.PP
PaperShell works locally and in Overleaf, uses LuaLaTeX to generate the correct
preamble automatically, and produces final sources that compile with pdfLaTeX,
so editors do not need any special tools.

.SS GENERAL VERBS
Most of PaperShell's operations start with a \fIverb\fR, optionally followed by
one or more \fInouns\fR.
.TP
\fBinit\fR [\fIfolder\fR]
Creates an empty document project in the current folder. If \fIfolder\fR is
speecified, initializes the project in this particular folder. Produces a
warning (and does nothing else) if a project is already initialized.
.TP
\fBexport\fR [\fI-f\fR] [\fI-i\fR] [\fI-z\fR] [\fIfolder\fR]
Exports the sources of the project to a folder called \fIExport\fR. The default
destination can be overridden by specifiying a \fIfolder\fR.
.RS
.TP
\fB-f\fR
Puts all files in a single (flat) folder without any subfolder. Adjusts the
relative paths in the main document accordingly.
.TP
\fB-i\fR
Resolves all calls to \fIinput\fR in the main document, and includes them
directly, thus creating a single compilable file.
.TP
\fB-z\fR
Zips the resulting bundle. Either 7zip or zip must be present in the path.
.RE

.SS LATEXMK VERBS
A few verbs in PaperShell are just calls to \fIlatexmk\fR. The main interest of
these verbs is that they can be run from any location inside the project
directory. Verbs for actions using latexmk are prefixed with \fImk\fR.
.TP
\fBmk\fR
Runs \fIlatexmk\fR on the main document.
.TP
\fBmk c\fR
Runs \fIlatexmk -c\fR on the main document, which has for effect of cleaning
all generated and temporary files.

.SS THEME VERBS
Verbs for actions pertaining to themes are prefixed with \fItx\fR.
.TP
\fBth list\fR
Lists available themes.
.TP
\fBth install\fR [<\fItheme\fR> | -f <\fIfile\fR>]
Installs a pre-packaged \fItheme\fR. If the -f option is not specified, defaults
to downloading the theme with given name from PaperShell's theme repository.
With the -f option, installs the theme from the local \fIfile\fR.
.TP
\fBth uninstall\fR <\fItheme\fR>
Deletes the files corresponding to \fItheme\fR.

.SS TEXTIDOTE VERBS
If TeXtidote is installed on the user's system, PaperShell can serve as a
front-end to call some of its common functions. Verbs for actions using
TeXtidote are prefixed with \fItx\fR.
.TP
\fBtx check\fR [\fI-b\fR]
Asks TeXtidote to analyze the document for grammar and spelling, using the
default language. The report is exported as an HTML file (default location:
\fItextidote.html\fR at the root of the project). The \fI-b\fR option opens the
resulting report in the system's default browser.
.TP
\fBtx wc\fR
Calculates an approximate word count on the main document. The text is first
stripped of all its LaTeX markup, and words are counted on that cleaned-up
version.

.SS LATEXDIFF VERBS
If \fIlatexdiff\fR is installed on the user's system, PaperShell can use it
to generate a version of the document that highlights the changes between the
current version of the paper and another version.
.TP
\fBld\fR <\fIold\fR> [\fItarget\fR]
Compares the document in \fIold\fR with the contents of the current project.
Folder \fIold\fR must point to the root of another PaperShell project, or any
subfolder thereof. The differences between the two projects are sent by default
to a folder called \fIDiff\fR in the current project. This can be overridden by
specifying \fItarget\fR.

.SH OVERRIDING DEFAULTS
Default values for parameters can be overridden by setting them in a file called
\fI.papershell\fR, located at the root of the project. For a new project, the
file simply reads like this:
.RS
.nf
return {
  version  = "3.x",
  initdate = "1955-11-12 22:04:00"
}
.fi
.RE
.P
The user can add other parameters to this file. Accepted keys are:
.RS
.TP
\fBmainfile\fR
The name of the file corresponding to the main document (default:
\fIpaper.tex\fR). 
.TP
\fBlanguage\fR
A two-letter language code, used by TeXtidote to check spelling and grammar
(default: \fIen\fR).
.RE

.SH SUPPORT
Support for PaperShell can be found on the GitHub repository at
<https://github.com/sylvainhalle/papershell>.
Bug reports and suggestions should be submitted via the issue tracker.

